{
  "analysis": "We now understand the frame saving: DG_DrawFrame saves /tmp/frame.bmp every 10 frames as a 32-bit BGRA BMP from DG_ScreenBuffer. The program uses an in-memory filesystem, so real syscalls are only used for doom.wad loading and stdout/stderr. We need the exact syscall constants and opcode distribution to build the interpreter.",
  "plan": "Gather the remaining critical information: all SYS_ constants from my_stdlib.c, the syscall dispatch code, the malloc/brk implementation, and the opcode distribution in the binary. Then I'll start implementing vm.js.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -nE \"#define SYS_\" doomgeneric/doomgeneric/my_stdlib.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk 'NR>=840 && NR<=900 {printf \"%4d %s\\n\", NR, $0}' doomgeneric/doomgeneric/my_stdlib.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk 'NR>=1530 && NR<=1565 {printf \"%4d %s\\n\", NR, $0}' doomgeneric/doomgeneric/my_stdlib.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -nE \"brk|sbrk|malloc|basic_malloc|heap|HEAP|_heap\" doomgeneric/doomgeneric/my_stdlib.c | head -40\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 - <<'PY'\nimport struct\nb=open('doomgeneric_mips','rb').read()\ntext_off=0; text_filesz=353556\ncounts={}\nsyscalls=[]\nfor off in range(0, text_filesz, 4):\n    w=struct.unpack_from('<I', b, text_off+off)[0]\n    op=w>>26\n    counts[op]=counts.get(op,0)+1\n    if op==0 and (w&0x3f)==0x0c:\n        syscalls.append(0x400000+off)\nprint('opcode distribution:')\nfor op,c in sorted(counts.items()):\n    print(f'  0x{op:02x} ({op:2d}): {c}')\nprint(f'\\\\nsyscall instructions: {len(syscalls)}')\nfor a in syscalls[:20]:\n    print(f'  0x{a:08x}')\nPY\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    }
  ]
}
